{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545277-archetypes-for-sorcerers-john-constantine","id":1545277,"title":"Archetypes for Sorcerers: John Constantine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-03T21:53:10-08:00","id":1545277,"title":"Archetypes for Sorcerers: John Constantine","content":"John Constantine has always been a child of the Nineties fandom....and Eighties. Hellblazer is as close to a collection of my all-time favorite comic books and fiction as a whole as I possess. When I was an edgy teenager, the character was against heaven and hell both as well as far more &quot;adult&quot; than any of the old comic book characters I'd used to read (Spider-Man and Batman). VERTIGO was one of the best things to ever happen to both comic books as well as DC comics as possible.<br /> <br /> John is a character the WOD kind of struggled to replicate, though.<br /> <br /> Part of the fun of John Constantine is that he's actually a ritualist and hedge wizard who doesn't throw around spells like Doctor Strange. In his own comic, he's an impressive mage but in the larger multiverse, he's no Zatanna (who functions more like a Mage: The Ascension Marauder). John primarily deals with demons and pagan gods (as well as the occasional demon) with his (presumed) 5 in Manipulation and Subterfuge scores.<br /> <br /> IMHO, Curseborne is almost (?) TAILOR MADE to do John Constantine faithfully. One of the biggest long-term character traits of John is that he's not motivated by a sense of heroism. Guilt, certainly, is there for the Newcastle incident (where he sent a little girl to Hell). However, he's also motivated by the fact that magic is used as an addiction and much better than Willow Rosenberg. He gets off on the power, occult energies, and the rush he gets from matching wits with the First of the Fallen or Gabriel.<br /> <br /> Perfect for Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Unburdened? Reeves? Unique? Not sure. I think he might even be Network.<br /> <br /> One of things that John also displays is the fact that he's constantly not paying the price for his magic. No, instead it's John's friends and assistant who always end up horribly dying as well as paying the supernatural price for his action. It's not even a theory since one of his most famous stories is him tricking one of his friends to allow himself to starve to death in order to banish a demon he's hosting.<br /> <br /> His family has also inherited the Constantine &quot;Curse&quot; by the fates of his parents, sister, and ancestor Joanna.<br /> <br /> What do you think are archetypal examples of other Lineages and Families?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T10:45:24-08:00","id":1545328,"title":"","content":"Ashton Kutcher character from the Butterfly Effect would fit under the cursed lineage as most of the males if his family could travel back points in there timeline and try to change things but always with heavy cost as the Dad pointed out that you can't change events without altering the people caught up in it. He would have lost moments in time as we later learned that it would be his older self hijacking him or that he would have new memories to go along with the old ones.<br /> <br /> It's no wonder that they would go mad and in his case in an alternative ending that he caused himself to die while still a fetus and break the cycle and saw that the curse would be broken with his mother giving birth to a daughter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}